%N A402440 a(n) = A402439(A102476(n)); largest k in [1,N] coprime to N such that k is a quadratic residue modulo N, N = A102476(n).
%C A402440 N = A102476(n) is the least number such that the multiplicative group of integers modulo N has 2^n square roots of 1.
%C A402440 a(n) is the largest element in row A102476(n) of A096103.
%C A402440 The smallest nonsquare k in [1,N] such that k is a quadratic residue modulo N is A002189(n-2) for n >= 6. (For n <= 5 no such nonsquare k in [1,N] exists since A102476(n) is in A303704).
%H A402440 Jianing Song, <a href="/A402440/b402440.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..52</a> (using data of A045535)
%F A402440 a(n) = A102476(n) - A045535(n-2) for n >= 2.
%e A402440 List of squares modulo N = 1, 3, 8, 24, 120, 840, 9240 in A102476:
%e A402440   1
%e A402440   1
%e A402440   1
%e A402440   1
%e A402440   1, 49
%e A402440   1, 121, 169, 289, 361, 529
%e A402440   1, 169, 289, 361, 529, 841, 961, 1369, 1681, 1849, 2209, 2641, 2689, 2809, 3481, 3529, 3721, 4321, 4489, 5041, 5329, 5569, 6169, 6241, 6889, 7561, 7681, 7921, 8089, 8761
%o A402440 (PARI) a(n) = if(n==0, 1, A402439( 4*factorback(primes(n-1)) )) \\ see A402439 for its program
